@copilot Update this PR directly on its existing head, `open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation:copilot/refsheads1`. Do not open another PR or rename or replace a branch. Keep any follow-up branch GitHub assigns.

In `Jms2InstrumentationTest` under `jms-1.1/javaagent/src/jms2Test` and `Jms3InstrumentationTest` under `jms-3.0/javaagent/src/test`, rename `asyncSendSuccessRestoresCallerContext` to `asyncSendCompletionUsesCallerContext`. Remove the pre/post-send `SpanContext` comparison and the `originalContext` snapshot/check outside `runWithSpan` in both success tests. The sender call should just be `testing.runWithSpan("parent", () -> producer.send(sentMessage, listener));`. Remove imports only if they become unused.

Keep the span started inside `onCompletion` and the trace assertion that it and the send span are siblings under `parent`, along with the latch, message ID, and existing telemetry assertions. The delayed-failure tests already assert caller restoration after normal return from this same `send` overload, before invoking `onException`. Leave those tests, production code, and the repository instruction files unchanged. Follow the repository's existing conventions and run the focused JMS 2 `jms2Test` and JMS 3 `test` cases if feasible.

